  "body": {
    "source_format": "markdown",
    "plain_text": "By Fermat's little theorem, 7^12 ≡ 1 mod 13. Since 100 = 8*12 + 4, we get 7^100 ≡ (7^12)^8 * 7^4 ≡ 7^4 mod 13. Now 7^2 = 49 ≡ 10 mod 13, so 7^4 ≡ 10^2 = 100 ≡ 9 mod 13.",
    "markdown": "By Fermat's little theorem, $7^{12} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{13}$. Since $100 = 8\\cdot12 + 4$, we get $7^{100} \\equiv (7^{12})^8 7^4 \\equiv 7^4 \\pmod{13}$. Now $7^2 = 49 \\equiv 10 \\pmod{13}$, so $7^4 \\equiv 10^2 = 100 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{13}$."
  },
